---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const privacyEmail = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_PRIVACY_EMAIL?.trim() || 'privacy@anchor.com';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="How Anchor processes personal data under GDPR, where EU data is stored, and how OpenAI is used."
  currentPath="/privacy"
>
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      This policy explains how Anchor (“we”) processes personal data for the OpenConf hackathon prototype. Controller
      contact: <a href={`mailto:${privacyEmail}`}>{privacyEmail}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      Anchor is a family memory product that helps practise spaced retrieval in a group chat. For privacy requests email{' '}
      {privacyEmail}.
    </p>

    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Account data: email, display name, account UUID.</li>
      <li>Consent records: acceptance of Terms and Privacy, optional marketing preference, timestamps (Neon).</li>
      <li>Family moments: text, photos, or voice notes you submit in the demo or via WhatsApp.</li>
      <li>Uploaded files: Blob objects plus Neon metadata keyed by account id.</li>
      <li>Technical logs needed to run the service (security, errors).</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Purposes and legal bases (GDPR)</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Contract / steps prior to contract</strong> — create and run your account and the demo.</li>
      <li><strong>Consent</strong> — optional marketing emails; acceptance of Terms/Privacy at signup.</li>
      <li><strong>Legitimate interests</strong> — secure the service, prevent abuse, improve the prototype (balanced against your rights).</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Where data is stored (EU sovereignty)</h2>
    <p>
      Account profiles, consent records, and file metadata are stored in <strong>Neon Postgres on AWS Frankfurt
      (<code>eu-central-1</code>)</strong>. Optional media assets use <strong>Vercel Blob in Frankfurt (<code>fra1</code>)</strong>.
    </p>

    <h2>Artificial intelligence (OpenAI)</h2>
    <p>
      To extract recallable moments, transcribe voice notes, and synthesise speech we send relevant text and audio to
      <strong>OpenAI’s API</strong> (<code>api.openai.com</code>). Prompts and media may be processed
      <strong>outside the European Union</strong> under OpenAI’s API terms. Do not submit special-category health data you
      are not prepared to share with that processor.
    </p>

    <h2>Processors</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Neon (Vercel Marketplace) — Postgres in EU <code>eu-central-1</code> (accounts, consents, file metadata, snapshots).</li>
      <li>Vercel — website, Nest API (Frankfurt), and Blob storage (<code>fra1</code>).</li>
      <li>OpenAI API — moment extraction, transcription, and speech (may process outside the EU).</li>
      <li>Twilio — WhatsApp delivery when connected.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Retention</h2>
    <p>
      Account and Neon data are kept while your account exists, or until you request deletion. Blob objects follow the same
      account lifetime. Anonymous in-memory demo state on the API may reset when the server restarts. Cached OpenAI answers
      on the API filesystem are ephemeral operational caches.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Under GDPR you may request access, rectification, erasure, restriction, portability, and objection, and you may
      withdraw consent where processing is consent-based. Contact {privacyEmail}. You may also lodge a complaint with your
      local supervisory authority.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>Anchor is not directed at children under 16. Do not create accounts for minors without lawful basis.</p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>We may update this policy for the hackathon prototype; the date in the page footer or git history reflects changes.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Privacy / GDPR: <a href={`mailto:${privacyEmail}`}>{privacyEmail}</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
